Add system tray presence and hide-to-tray

Give FreeFlow the always-available background presence of the macOS menu-bar
app. Win32 TrayIcon (Shell_NotifyIcon + window subclass) shows a notification
icon with an Open / Settings / Quit context menu. Closing the main window now
hides it to the tray (AppWindow.Closing canceled) so the global shortcuts keep
running in the background; Quit performs the real exit and cleanup.

- TrayIcon uses a 32/64-bit-safe SetWindowLongPtr wrapper (x86 only exports
  SetWindowLongW) and TrackPopupMenu with TPM_RETURNCMD for synchronous menu
  handling, loading the app .ico for the tray glyph.
- App wires tray events to show/settings/quit on the UI dispatcher.

Verified: portable x86 launches clean (no crash log) with tray + overlay +
sounds startup wiring.

